  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/506caa58-1b83-4992-a386-03e56b74e5e5.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.45833in;height:0.63333in\"> <br/><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is weaker ligand than <math><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  <br/>So, <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math>  <br/>Since, oxidation number of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> in the complex <br/><math><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><munder><mrow><mtext>Cr</mtext><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mtext>x0</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi></mi></math> is calculated as, <math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></munder></math>  <br/>So, <math><mtext>C</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> has <math><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> configuration <br/>Similarly, oxidation no. of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> in <br/><math><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><munder><mrow><mtext>Cr</mtext><mo>(</mo><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mtext>x0</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> <math><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is calculated as, <math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext></mtext></mrow></munder></math>  <br/>So  <math><mtext>C</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  has <math><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> configuration <br/>Thus, both A and B are paramagnetic with 3 unpaired electrons. <br/>We know, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>absorbed</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>  <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/9eb0b9fd-f651-4cac-8db8-d4b322644f23.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.66667in;height:1.33333in\"> <br/>Since <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math>  <br/><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math>  <br/>A is violet coloured so its energy is calculated from yellow colour absorbed. <br/><math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math> or <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>violet</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>yellow</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>  <br/>Similarly, <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> or <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>yellow</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>yellow</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>  <br/>Hence, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> values of A and B are calculated from the energies of yellow and violet light respectively.",
